xrefpairs_rv32 -- the RV32 ELF fixture for `kuna xrefs` over an address a
register pair forms (decompiler/crates/kuna-cli/tests/xrefs_address_pairs.rs).

What it is
  A 14,588-byte static RV32 ELF linked at 0x10000 from xrefpairs.c at -O0 (lui +
  lw, lui + sw and lui + addi of a label and a global, the shapes clang emits
  for non-PIC code) and xrefpairs_riscv.S (lui + lw, lui + addi, lui + sw,
  auipc + addi, auipc + ld/lw, and two lui bases meeting at a join, which must
  NOT compose).

Why it is vendored
  The pairs depend on the code model and on linker relaxation (which rewrites
  them against gp when it can), so the binary is checked in rather than built
  at test time.

Where it came from
  Ubuntu clang 14.0.0 compiles, LLD 23.1.4 (docker image mstorsjo/llvm-mingw)
  links:

      clang --target=riscv32-unknown-elf -march=rv32imafdc -mabi=ilp32d \
          -O0 -fno-pic -ffreestanding -mno-relax -c xrefpairs.c -o a.o
      clang --target=riscv32-unknown-elf -march=rv32imafdc -mabi=ilp32d \
          -c xrefpairs_riscv.S -o b.o
      ld.lld -static -nostdlib -e main --build-id=none --no-relax a.o b.o \
          -o xrefpairs_rv32

  sha256 1339bfeb689dc57aa3552c6273c8b8874037130441ac19bf133fd286aa52e504.
  Never executed.
